-- title:
--   Node thickness (p-1)·width at supersingular points of X₀(pM)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M \ge 5$ with $p \nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $\{p\}$ and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K_2$ be the intermediate field of $L \subset L((q))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise images of the field $\mathbb{Q}$-generated by the ratios $f/g$ of $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight for $\Gamma_0(Mp)$ having integral $q$-expansions. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $\varpi$ a generator of the maximal ideal, and let $A$ act on $K_2$ compatibly with $L$. Let $j_2 \in K_2$ be the element whose Laurent series is the image of the $q$-expansion of $j$ under the coefficient map, assumed nonzero. Write $\mathcal{X}_2 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K₂ j₂`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ of `chartAlgFin` (elements of $K_2$ integral over $A[j_2]$) and `chartAlgInf` (those integral over $A[j_2^{-1}]$) along the middle chart. Let $z_2$ be a point of $\mathcal{X}_2$ at which the germ of $\varpi$, pulled back along the structure morphism $\mathcal{X}_2 \to \operatorname{Spec} A$, lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, let $y_2$ be a prime $\mathfrak{y}_2$ of `chartAlgFin` whose image in $\mathcal{X}_2$ is $z_2$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $\mathfrak{y}_2$, the value $\varphi(j_2)$ lies in `ssJSet p Ω`, that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $p$. Then there exist an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $p$ each of whose elements satisfies $x^{p^n} = x$ for some $n > 0$; a place $w$ of `modularFunctionFieldC k M` (a proper valuation subring containing $k$ whose ideals are principal) lying in `ssPlaces p M k`, so $w$ is rational, an affine geometric place, and $w$'s residue value at `jGeomGen k M` is supersingular; and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from `chartAlgFin` to `modularFunctionFieldC k M` with $\rho(\varpi) = 0$, $\rho(j_2) =$ `jGeomGen k M`, whose image lies in the valuation subring of $w$, with $\rho(b)$ a nonunit of that subring exactly when $b \in \mathfrak{y}_2$, and such that every element of `modularFunctionFieldC k M` is a ratio $a/b$ with $a, b$ in the $k$-subalgebra generated by the range of $\rho$ and $b \ne 0$; and furthermore a complete discrete valuation domain $W_2$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma_2 : A \to W_2$ with maximal ideal generated by $\sigma_2(\varpi)$, and a ring isomorphism $$\widehat{\mathcal{O}}_{\mathcal{X}_2, z_2} \;\cong\; W_2[[X_0, X_1]]\big/\bigl(X_0X_1 - \sigma_2(\varpi)^{(p-1)\cdot \mathrm{placeWidthChar}(p, M, w)}\bigr),$$ the completion being the adic completion of the stalk at its maximal ideal, carrying the germ of each $a \in A$ to the constant $\sigma_2(a)$. Here $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}(p, M, w)$ is $\mathrm{jWidthChar}$ of the residue value $w(\mathtt{jGeomGen})$ ($12$ or $1$ according as that value is $0$ or not when $p = 2$, $6$ or $1$ when $p = 3$, and $\mathrm{jWidth}$ otherwise) divided by the ramification $\mathrm{ord}_w$ of `jGeomGen` minus its residue value.
--
--   This is the local structure of the integral model of $X_0(pM)$ at a supersingular point of the fibre over $p$: an ordinary double point over a complete discrete valuation ring, of thickness $(p-1)$ times the characteristic-$p$ width of the corresponding supersingular place of the level-$M$ function field, in the classical form of Deligne–Rapoport and Katz–Mazur. It is used in the study of the model of $X_0(pM)$ at level prime to $p$, where the exponent is re-expressed through the inertia at the supersingular point.
